#14004
"Dead End of a Trail"
"You are on a small trail that reaches its end northward, obstructed by an
immense marble gate partially covered in ivy.  The grass have grown to several
feet here, unmaintained and overflowing with weeds.  Inhabiting the east and
west are thickets of underbrush and shrubbery that seem to be fighting for
every inch of space among them.  A stone boulder rests southward.
"
""
