#14010
"Repair Shop"
"Upon entering this tiny shop, your senses are assailed with the scents of
saddle-soap, hot metal, and leather.  Low benches and work tables lie
scattered about in a seemingly random order, each piled high with unfinished
projects and strange devices.  Great care must be taken to avoid stumbling
over the numerous barrels of rivets, scrap leather, and other various odds and
ends.  The proprietor, however, moves nimbly about the cluttered shop with an
air of comfortable familiarity.  The shop is open to the elements on all
sides, with thick brush seen to the east and west.  The mountain peaks loom
overhead to the north, enshrouded in mist, and the shining sea of stars can be
viewed off to the south.
"
""
